# tine — a reusable buck2 cell: the format-neutral machinery for building a
# distribution from source (rules in defs/rules, the rpm format plugin + drivers
# in distribution/rpm, the vendored sandbox in distribution). It carries no
# distribution *data* — a consuming project supplies that (its manifest + lock +
# package targets) and instantiates the rules with it.
#
# A consumer registers this directory as the `tine` cell in its root .buckconfig
# (`[cells] tine = <path>`); the cell self-references as `@tine//…` (see the
# qualified attr defaults in defs/rules). No sections here on purpose: the cell
# inherits the consuming project's parser/build/platform config.
